nano7kit licensing
==================

nano7kit's own code is MIT (see LICENSE). That covers host/, install,
start, scripts/, tests/, docs/, pocketjs/, games/fruitninja/, the
nano7kit apps under nanoapps/ (Lap, Free RAM, JS Hero, JS Samples,
JS QuickJS, JS Hello) and the installer.

Exceptions:

  games/pvz_portable/          LGPL-3.0-or-later (PvZ-Portable engine)
  nanoapps/sdk/, nanoapps/vendor/, nanoapps/tools/,
  nanoapps/system/silver_resident_na/
                               NanoApps (nfzerox), MIT; the launcher fork
                               keeps that licence and notice
  upstream/*.patch             changes to nano7-untethered files (including
                               the wInd3x patch, GPL-2.0); each hunk follows
                               the licence of the file it changes
  untether/artifacts/extra/    prebuilt apps; each keeps its source's
                               licence. The texts are in LICENSES/:
                               PocketJS MIT, QuickJS MIT, Inter OFL-1.1
                               (also next to the font at
                               untether/artifacts/extra/Data/PocketJS/fonts/LICENSE.txt),
                               Font Awesome Free 7.2.0, dlmalloc public domain / CC0.
                               See LICENSES/README.md.

Not in this repository, fetched at pinned commits (UPSTREAM.txt) when
you install or build:

  nano7-untethered (olievans123)   loader, Blocks, Game Boy, Probe and the
                                   Mario 64 / Mario Kart 64 ports; no
                                   licence stated, so not redistributed here
  NanoApps (nfzerox)               MIT, inside nano7-untethered
  ipod_sun_untethered (nfzerox)    GPL-3.0, inside nano7-untethered; the
                                   firmware builder runs it on your Mac
  wInd3x (freemyipod)              GPL-2.0, built from source
  PvZ-Portable (wszqkzqk)          LGPL-3.0-or-later
  PocketJS (pocket-nexus)          MIT
  Temple Run, Flappy Bird and Doodle Jump ports (olievans123), no licence
  stated, fetched only when you build that game

nano7-untethered files are checked one by one against the sha256 list
in upstream/lock.json.

There is no Apple firmware, ROM, ipa or game data in this repository.
The firmware builder downloads Apple's iPod nano 1.1.2 firmware from
Apple on your machine. Games need your own files.
